{"id":77444872354975,"type":"album","name":"Aquemini","artist":"OutKast","year":1998,"weight":57,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710806.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-63f4592c-6f58-32bb-bd9f-a431dc14e04d/mbid-63f4592c-6f58-32bb-bd9f-a431dc14e04d-6640977411.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":16,"country":"US","aoty":90,"aoty_user":90,"sputnik":4.42,"yt":"vnnTW6WL7pw","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/outkast/aquemini","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/2915-outkast-aquemini.php","sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/8171/OutKast-Aquemini/"},"desc":"A vaguely futuristic, synthesizer-drenched album punctuated with anthemic choruses and bluesy beats, Aquemini addresses numerous topics such as emancipation, drug addiction and problematic relationships, while exploring the bleakest aspects of humanity. In contrast to much of hip hop music in the late 1990s, OutKast did not tone down the regional qualities, like the harmonica break on \"Rosa Parks\" and distinctive Atlanta slang and diction throughout. \"Rosa Parks\" was later nominated for the 1999 Grammy Award for Best Rap Performance by a Duo or Group. The song led to much controversy with Rosa Parks filing a defamation suit against OutKast. Aquemini ."},"artist_ref":{"id":41193432502071,"name":"OutKast","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/2014227235242_2014-08-15_Rock%27n%27Heim_-_Sven_-_5D_MK_II_-_250_-_IMG_0063_mod.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":136937573393074,"type":"genre","name":"hip hop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1554,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":50890778952785,"type":"genre","name":"Dirty South","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":222,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":196943961983090,"type":"genre","name":"alternative hip hop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":48,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":207755761847598,"type":"genre","name":"Hardcore","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":540,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":1